 "level_notes": {"0": "Several independent, conforming implementations exist: MLton (whole-program optimising), SML/NJ (interactive, incremental), Poly/ML, MLKit (region-based memory), Moscow ML, HaMLet (a direct transcription of the Definition) and the verified CakeML dialect.", "1": "The language is defined by The Definition of Standard ML (Revised) (Milner, Tofte, Harper, MacQueen; MIT Press 1997), a formal natural-semantics specification; the SML family site hosts open PDFs with the publisher's permission. The Definition is a single PDF without stable section anchors, so concept deep links at level 1 point to the SML Basis Library pages instead.", "3": "Wikipedia and PLDB cover SML; Rosetta Code reports 'blocked' from the research sandbox."},
